     "text": "Plan step 0: ev_query_telemetry_1 and ev_detect_change_points_1 show ST30-WLD air_pressure_bar dropped to a minimum of 4.95 bar (mean 5.3393 bar, std 0.18986 bar, 43.63% outside normal [5.3, 5.9] bar), with a ramp change point beginning at 2026-08-07T11:00:15Z (before_mean 5.6002 bar, after_mean 5.0167 bar, delta -0.58349 bar), verifying an actual low pressure condition. Data quality: 0.61% missing, 0 gaps, 0 stuck periods.\nPlan step 1: ev_query_telemetry_2, ev_detect_change_points_2, and ev_detect_change_points_3 show UT-AIR header_pressure_bar dropped below 6.0 bar (mean 5.5922 bar, min 5.22 bar, max 5.99 bar, 100% outside normal [6, 7.5] bar) with a ramp change point from 2026-08-07T12:20:15Z to 14:05:15Z (delta -1.6979 bar down to 5.4213 bar), while compressor_current_a loaded_fraction reached 1.0 (mean 92.024 A, change point at 09:58:15Z rising from duty fraction 0.58439 to 1.0) and oil_temp_c averaged 82.387 degC (normal [60, 85] degC), confirming a plant-wide utility compressed air supply deficit. Data quality: missing 1.11%-1.58%, 0 gaps, 0 stuck periods.\nPlan step 2: ev_query_telemetry_3 and ev_detect_change_points_4 show upstream ST20-WLD air_pressure_bar concurrently dropped below 5.3 bar (min 4.97 bar, mean 5.3412 bar, 43.66% outside normal [5.3, 5.9] bar) with a ramp change point beginning at 2026-08-07T10:52:15Z (delta -0.53808 bar to after_mean 5.0611 bar), confirming a common header supply issue rather than an ST30-isolated leak. Data quality: 1.21%-1.58% missing, 0 gaps, 0 stuck periods.\nPlan step 3: ev_query_telemetry_1, ev_detect_change_points_1, and ev_spectrum_1 show ST30-WLD air_pressure_bar exhibits smooth continuous ramp behavior down to ~4.95-5.02 bar with no drops to zero/null, 0 stuck periods, and low-amplitude spectral peaks (top peak 0.0127 Hz, amplitude 0.003905 bar), refuting a sensor flatline, disconnect, or wiring fault.\nPlan step 4: ev_query_telemetry_1 shows ST30-WLD cycle_time_s (mean 50.056 s, max 50.8 s vs [46,